      "id": "95apmo1",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Montane Forest Altitudinal Zones"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Montane forests are categorized by altitudinal zones ranging from subtropical to alpine vegetation.",
        "Coniferous forests occur at elevations between 3000–4000 m, while alpine vegetation is found above 4000 m.",
        "Mangroves possess pneumatophores which serve as specialized breathing roots.",
        "Vivipary is a key adaptation where seeds germinate while still attached to the parent tree.",
        "Salt filtration mechanisms help mangroves survive in saline environment conditions."
      ],
      "id": "s7a7lm6"
    },
    {
      "type": "pullQuote",
      "content": "Vivipary – seeds germinate while attached to parent tree.",
      "id": "zoodkt7"
